1. What this edition is based on
---------------------------------

Companion OS in this directory is built on CachyOS. That is a statement of fact. On the surfaces this overlay owns (the ISO file
name, the volume label, the boot menus, the installer window, the desktop, the login screen, the hostname and /etc/os-release)
the only descriptive use of the CachyOS name is the VARIANT field of /etc/os-release ("Plasma (based on CachyOS)"); they say
Companion OS everywhere else. Developer documentation and code comments in this repository (this file, the READMEs, the
architecture document, comments in scripts) name CachyOS descriptively and are not product surfaces. The identifiers that keep
the name on purpose are in section 5.

  * CachyOS-Live-ISO, https://github.com/CachyOS/CachyOS-Live-ISO, GPL-3.0 (the LICENSE file of that repository). The build
    uses it unmodified at a pinned commit (upstream.lock: UPSTREAM_SHA) and applies the overlay to a copy.
  * archiso (mkarchiso, mkinitcpio-archiso), GPL-3.0-or-later, run unmodified from the Arch Linux repositories.
  * cachyos-calamares-next, the CachyOS build of Calamares, GPL-3.0-or-later (its PKGBUILD); the installer in the live image is
    that package, configured by the overlay in installer/.
  * The packages the image is made of (Arch Linux, CachyOS, and the NVIDIA userspace the live list contains) are installed from
    the repositories at build time and carry their own licences. The image is not a fork of any of them.

2. Files in this tree that derive from, or sit next to, GPL-3.0 material
-------------------------------------------------------------------------

What a file's own text says is stated per file, because the headers are the thing a recipient will read. Of the files in 2a none
carries a licence or copyright line of its own, so for them this notice is the only record. The lists are the ones known when
this notice was written; `git log --follow` and the upstream commit in upstream.lock are the way to check a derivation.
iso/tests/overlay-brand.sh (part E) checks that every path named below exists, that no file under 2a to 2c carries a licence line
that contradicts its list, and that the CC0 header in 2d is still the one the file has.

2a. Derived from GPL-3.0 files. Treat these as GPL-3.0-or-later, not as Lifescope-only files.

  * iso/overlay/patches/0001-grub-companion-os-menu.patch: modification of upstream's archiso/grub/grub.cfg and grub/loopback.cfg.
  * iso/overlay/patches/0002-syslinux-companion-os-menu.patch: modification of upstream's archiso/syslinux/*.cfg (the comment
    lines at its top are ours and carry no licence line).
  * iso/overlay/files/airootfs/usr/local/bin/calamares-online.sh: replaces upstream's script of the same name; it keeps its
    sequence (keyring refresh, installer package, start through pkexec-wrapper) and some of its comments.
  * iso/overlay/files/airootfs/etc/ssh/sshd_config.d/10-archiso.conf: replaces upstream's three-line file of the same name (the
    same two directives with the opposite values; the comments are ours).
  * iso/overlay/files/airootfs/etc/cachyos-release: modified copy of upstream's file of the same name (the same four keys,
    other values).
  * installer/modules/netinstall.yaml: the package groups of the pinned installer's own netinstall.yaml, trimmed (its header
    says which). Neither the original nor this copy has a licence line.
  * iso/scripts/in-container/20-build.sh: sources upstream's util-msg.sh and util-iso.sh at build time and replays their
    generators (the file cites util-iso.sh line numbers). It is original code that runs GPL code, which makes the build a
    combined work while it runs.

2b. CC0-1.0 templates, modified by us. Each file has `SPDX-License-Identifier: CC0-1.0` in its header. Upstream's counterparts
carry the same line (read in the research copy of the pinned installer's source on 2026-10-15; that copy is not in this
repository), so these headers are upstream's, kept. They are listed because the content was modified from CachyOS's
configuration; the CC0 dedication itself imposes nothing. The two shellprocess_ci_os_* files were written for this edition on
the shape of upstream's shellprocess template and carry its header. The installer as a whole is GPL-3.0-or-later; whether a
configuration file derived from it keeps its own CC0 grant is for counsel.

  * installer/settings.conf
  * installer/modules/*.conf
  * installer/branding/companion/branding.desc
  * installer/branding/companion/stylesheet.qss

2c. Original code of this repository, named here because it ships next to GPL code or could be mistaken for derived code.
It is headed "© Companion Intelligence — Lifescope Inc", carries no GPL notice and derives from no GPL file.

  * iso/overlay/files/airootfs/usr/lib/systemd/system-generators/companion-vm-timeouts: the slow-boot generator for virtual
    machines (it writes three systemd drop-ins). It is shipped in the ISO.
  * iso/tests/qemu-boot.sh: holds the identical text of that generator (`--vm-fixes`); not shipped.

2d. Open: the header and the upstream licence disagree.

  * installer/branding/companion/show.qml: its header says CC0-1.0, but upstream's show.qml of the same name carries
    GPL-3.0-or-later (the Calamares authors). Ours keeps its skeleton (the Presentation element, the slide timer and the slide
    functions of the Calamares QML API); the text and the images are ours. Until counsel decides, treat it as GPL-3.0-or-later;
