3. Redistribution of the ISO
-----------------------------

An ISO contains GPL and other copyleft binaries from Arch Linux and CachyOS packages (the kernel, the C library, KDE, ...).
Giving the ISO to a third party obliges us to give the corresponding source or a written offer for it. The build records what is
needed to do that: `<iso>.pkgs.txt` (every package with its version) and `<iso>.build-info` (the pins). A source offer is not
written yet. The live list also contains the proprietary NVIDIA userspace (`nvidia-utils`) from the repositories; its
redistribution terms have not been reviewed.

4. What we do not ship
-----------------------

No CachyOS artwork. In particular none of these is copied into this tree or into the image by the overlay:

  * the CachyOS wallpapers (package `cachyos-wallpapers`: not in the live package list), the CachyOS logo and marks,
  * the CachyOS GRUB theme (package `cachyos-grub-theme`; the installer's post-install step tries to remove it from the installed
    system and logs a warning if it can not),
  * the CachyOS Plymouth animation (`cachyos-plymouth-bootanimation`, `cachyos-plymouth-theme`),
  * the upstream boot-menu background: archiso/grub/splash.png and archiso/syslinux/splash.png of the pinned upstream commit
    (sha256 b5a6e75af70a2750438a780e68cc89f6106d205b88c79150db5686825420aa11) are replaced by images rendered from the Companion
    OS brand canon at build time; `iso/scripts/verify-iso.sh` compares the hash of every boot-menu image with it.

The artwork of the CachyOS packages that the image installs for other reasons (for example the logo inside a package's own icon
theme) is not ours to remove from those packages and is not used by the Companion OS surfaces. Our own brand assets come only
from vendor/brand and CI-Common, are rendered at build time by core/render/* and are not committed as binaries. The Manrope font
is OFL-1.1 (vendor/brand/fonts/LICENSE-Manrope.txt).

5. Names and marks
-------------------

  * CachyOS: no trademark or branding policy was found when this was researched (2026-10-15); the site's terms of service cover
    the forum and services. The absence of a page is not a permission. Before the CachyOS name is used in a file name, a
    product name, marketing or a store listing, ask the CachyOS maintainers in writing. The GPL is a copyright licence and gives
    no right to a project's name or logo.
  * Arch Linux: the trademark policy (terms.archlinux.org, the version dated 2021-04-18 as read on 2026-10-15) allows saying that
    a product is based on or derived from Arch Linux and does not allow using the marks to name the product. `ID_LIKE=arch` in
    /etc/os-release is a technical identifier, as CachyOS ships it. Commercial use of the marks needs a licence from Arch.
  * Identifiers that keep the CachyOS name on purpose: `ID=cachyos` in /etc/os-release, package, repository and unit names
    (`linux-cachyos`, `[cachyos]`, `cachyos-*`), kernel version strings, and the `-cachyos` suffix of `uname -r`. They are
    identifiers that tools match on, not branding. The image says so in docs; it does not hide it.

